    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Extract the following fields from the given contract email and PDF text:\n\n- Client Name\n- Contract Number\n- Effective Date\n- Contract Value\n- PDF URL (if available)\n- Source Email\n\nHere is the email body:\n{{ $json.snippet }}\n\nHere is the PDF text:\n{{ $json.text }}\n\nReturn only a JSON object with the extracted values, following the schema provided.\n\nEmail from: {{ $json.From }}\nEmail Subject: {{ $json.Subject }}\nEmail date: {{ $json.headers.date }}\n\n\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are an AI assistant connected to a Supabase database. \nYou analyze email and PDF contract data, then insert structured records into the 'contracts' table using the Supabase tool.\n\nThe 'contracts' table fields are:\n- id (uuid, auto-generated)\n- email_subject (text)\n- email_from (text)\n- email_date (timestamp)\n- email_body (text)\n- contract_number (text)\n- contract_value (numeric)\n- client_name (text)\n- contract_date (date, format YYYY-MM-DD)\n- pdf_filename (text)\n- pdf_content (text)\n- extracted_date (timestamp, auto defaults to now)\n\nRules:\n1. Always extract as much detail as possible from the email and PDF. \n2. Insert the data directly into the 'contracts' table using the Supabase tool.\n3. Do not return plain text or JSON in your reply; the record must be saved in Supabase.\n4. If any field is missing, insert an empty string or null (except id and extracted_date which are auto-handled).\n"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        768,
        -16
      ],
      "id": "9a2f05a9-afcc-47dc-b585-168797d12f7f",
